,"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","displayTopic":"Labor and Delivery · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-e9ff69fc585b","stem":"Mention any five (5) qualities of a leader Establishes and communicates goals Creates shared vision and commitment Competent, confident and caring Visible, positive, optimistic Honors all commitments Risk-taker and problem solver Seeks mutually beneficial solutions Admits Errors/Failures Innovates and develops","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-5cbf95201fb2","stem":"Mention any five (5) organizational functions Organizing Planning Directing/coordinates Controlling Decision Making","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-07ee768b82b5","stem":"Mention any five (5) qualities of a Manager Maintains control of operations by meeting operational standards Assures high testing quality and customer service Assures staff compliance with policies and procedures Accomplishes goals; makes good decisions Manages resources effectively including time Administers and maintains Focuses on the present realistic situation Focuses on systems and structures Day to day operations Managers are people who do things right","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-7ad22b8e0048","stem":"Mention Factors that may lead in Poor Decision Making Not enough information Emotion-based decisions Not enough input from others Lack of experience with the problem Fear of consequences of making the wrong decision Poor implementation/communications SECTION D: ESSAY QUESTION: (20 MARKS) Instructions This section consists of two (2) questions which are supposed to be answered in a narrative way Bulleting and numbering are NOT ALLOWED. Write your answer on the empty pages of this question paper Each question should start on a new page","type":"Essay / Structured Essay","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-bb6eac624696","stem":"Describe the 6 qualities of an effective Manager. (10 Marks) Introduction (0.5 Marks ) A Manager is the person responsible for planning and directing the work of a group of individuals, monitoring their work, and taking corrective action when necessary. Managers may direct workers directly or they may direct several supervisors who direct the workers. MAIN BODY (9 Marks)1.5@ Maintains control of operations by meeting operational standards Assures high testing quality and customer service Assures staff compliance with policies and procedures Accomplishes goals; makes good decisions Manages resources effectively including time Administers and maintains Focuses on the present realistic situation Focuses on systems and structures Day to day operations Managers are people who do things right Conclusion ( 0.5 Marks) SECTION E: SCENARIO BASED QUESTION: (30 MARKS Instructions This section consists of three (3) scenario-based questions. Each question supposed to be answered as per guided case scenario Bulleting and numbering are NOT ALLOWED. Write your answer on the empty pages of this question paper Each question should start on a new page","type":"Clinical Vignette","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-7525a126a34c","stem":"Which principle of management is focused on ensuring that different parts of the organization work together harmoniously? o A) Coordinating o B) Controlling o C) Commanding o D) Organizing o ) Coordinating","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-c8f37de4f2e9","stem":"What is the purpose of an organogram in an organization? o A) To show the location of departments o B) To indicate lines of communication o C) To define the span of control o D) All of the above o ) All of the above","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-f342d31df146","stem":"Which function of management involves supervising, guiding, motivating, and leading people towards the attainment of planned targets? o A) Organizing o B) Planning o C) Directing o D) Controlling o ) Directing","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-154c0f17ed82","stem":"What is the primary responsibility of the laboratory manager in prioritizing tasks? o A) Establishing a chain of command o B) Allocating resources o C) Setting clear priorities o D) Delegating authority o ) Setting clear priorities","type":"Short Answer","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-21874f7b825c","stem":"What is the main purpose of planning in an organization? o A) To establish a chain of command o B) To clarify the process of attaining desired goals o C) To supervise and guide employees o D) To measure performance against standards o ) To clarify the process of attaining desired goals","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAn