aft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-8a36eee07fe8","stem":"Which factor is NOT typically associated with poor decision-making?  A) Not enough information  B) Emotion-based decisions  C) Involvement of people closest to the action  D) Lack of experience with the problem  ) Involvement of people closest to the action","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-c34d26499bd9","stem":"What is the key aspect of delegation in management?  A) Avoiding accountability  B) Tracking and managing all projects  C) Centralizing decision-making  D) Blaming subordinates for failures  ) Tracking and managing all projects","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-57438920fa25","stem":"Which management function involves supervising, guiding, motivating, and leading people towards the attainment of planned targets?  A) Organizing  B) Planning  C) Directing  D) Controlling  ) Directing","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-647f0a2e4f5c","stem":"What is the purpose of a Gantt chart?  A) To list all actions/steps needed for a project, along with deadlines and responsible individuals  B) To establish lines of communication  C) To clarify the process of attaining desired goals  D) To visualize tasks, their start dates, duration, and dependencies  ) To visualize tasks, their start dates, duration, and dependencies • What is the primary purpose of an organogram in an organization? • n organogram helps to illustrate the levels of authority, lines of communication, reporting structures, and responsibilities within an organization. • Define the term \"delegation\" in the context of management. • elegation is the process of assigning authority and responsibility to another person to empower them to make decisions and complete tasks on behalf of the delegator. • Why is planning essential in an organization? • helps in making advanced rational decisions about the future, and ensures efficient use of resources. • What is the purpose of controlling in management? • ontrolling ensures that the organization is moving in the desired direction and progress is being made towards the achievement of goals by measuring performance against standards and taking corrective action when necessary. • Briefly explain the directing function of management. • irecting involves supervising, guiding, motivating, and leading people towards the attainment of planned targets by issuing orders, overseeing work, motivating employees, communicating effectively, and influencing behavior. • What does the term \"authority\" refer to in management? • uthority is the power and right of a person to use and allocate resources efficiently, make decisions, and give orders to achieve organizational objectives. • Why is delegation important in management? • elegation is important because it empowers subordinates to make decisions, facilitates coordination of activities, helps in managing workload effectively, and fosters skill development and career growth. • What factors contribute to good decision-making in management? • ood decision-making involves getting all the facts, involving people closest to the action, having a good implementation strategy, communicating decisions effectively, and having knowledge of the job. • Describe the purpose of a Gantt chart. • Gantt chart is used to visualize tasks, their start dates, duration, and dependencies in a project, helping in planning, scheduling, and tracking progress. • What is the main function of an action planning grid? • for a project, along with responsible individuals, start dates, due dates, and status updates, facilitating organized project management and tracking.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"review","flags":["probable_document_or_multiple_questions","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["long_stem_manual_review","prior_structural_review_flag","probable_document_or_multiple_questions","subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-82bb2f8bc4ac","stem":"Who stated that leadership is \"the ability of a superior to influence the behaviors of his subordinates and persuade them to follow a particular course of action\"? • A) Chester Barnard • B) Frederick Taylor • C) Peter Drucker • D) Henry Fayol • ) Chester Barnard","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-1985f40bde3f","stem":"What is the primary focus of autocratic leadership? • A) Employee empowerment • B) Employee participation • C) Centralized decision-making • D) Delegating authority • ) Centralized decision-making","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasS