Accurate measurements are via analysis E Patients with occult hypoperfusion for of blood drawn from a line placed in more than 12 hours have a significantly the superior vena cava (SVC). higher mortality rate. D Levels below 50 per cent indicate inadequate oxygen delivery consistent TRANSFUSION ➜Resuscitation in shock with hypovolaemic shock. E High mixed venous saturation levels are 7. Which of the following statements are seen in sepsis. BLOOD false? A Administration of inotropic agents to an AND empty heart will help to increase diastolic ➜Reactionary haemorrhage filling and coronary perfusion. 10. Which of the following about B In all cases, regardless of classification, reactionary haemorrhage are false? SHOCK hypovolaemia and preload must be A This is delayed haemorrhage occurring 2: addressed first. within 24 h after operation. C Long, wide-bore catheters allow rapid B It is usually caused by dislodgement of infusion of fluids. clot, normalisation of blood pressure or D The oxygen-carrying capacity of both slippage of ligature. colloids and crystalloids is zero. C It is associated with infection. E Hypotonic solutions are poor volume D It can be significant, requiring expanders and should not be used in re-exploration. shock except in conditions of free water E It is usually venous. loss or sodium overload. ➜Blood transfusion ➜Inotropic support in shock 11. Which of the following about blood","type":"Clinical Vignette","subject":"Emergency Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"review","flags":["probable_document_or_multiple_questions","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Emergency Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["long_stem_manual_review","possible_multiple_questions_in_stem",