aging in the acute ➜Imaging in oncology abdomen 7. Which of the following statements 6. Which of the following statements are about oncological imaging are true? IMAGING false with regard to imaging of the A Early disease is best staged by acute abdomen? endoscopic US. A US is a good first-line investigation. B Accurate preoperative nodal involvement B CT is the best investigation for acute is not possible. DIAGNOSTIC diverticulitis. C Liver and lung metastases are best C Plain X-ray of KUB ( kidney, ureter, detected by US and CT. 10: bladder) is the best imaging for D Intraoperative US is used in liver suspected ureteric colic. resection. D US and CT can diagnose the cause and site of bowel obstruction. E Plain X-ray is the first-line investigation for suspected perforation or obstruction. Answers: Multiple choice questions ➜Hazards of imaging and radiation","type":"Radiological Interpretation","subject":"Radiography and Medical Imaging","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"review","flags":["topic_generic","requires_visual_review"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":true,"displaySubject":"Radiography and Medical Imaging","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["possible_multiple_questions_in_stem","prior_structural_review_flag","requires_visual_review","topic_generic","visual_asset_not_transcribed"],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-34b54946533f","stem":"Regarding sedation during endoscopy, before a colonoscopic polypectomy. which of the following statements are D Verbal consent for an endoscopy is false? acceptable practice. A Sedation has no significant dangers and E Perforation and haemorrhage are can be used without restrictions. uncommon but significant complications B All sedated patients require secure