 it. From social distancing, working from home (WFH) and panic buying, life took a sudden turn for the worse. New studies are popping up to show the benefits and concerns of social distancing and remote working (Robinson 2020). Licensed under Creative Common Page 375 ©Author(s) Remote-working also referred to as telecommuting or working from home, is an initiative that has been with us for a while. However, many organizations are yet to design and implement policies on remote-working. Recently, remote-working initiative has become a game changer, after the Coronavirus COVID 19 pandemic threatened to negatively impact on the productivity of many organizations. This has necessitated all organizations that are focused on remaining relevant in the business environment to modify their policies in order to accommodate remote-working. It has however been very challenging for a number of organizations to adjust","type":"Clinical Vignette","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-140313effa29","stem":"Mason, B. (2020). Is remote working really so bad?","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-0f39d4e0ced5","stem":"6 Apoptotic cells usually exhibit distinctive morphological features. Which one of the following morphological features is usually seen in pure apoptosis?","type":"Short Answer","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-5f53aa5c5bb3","stem":"7 A histopathologist reports fat necrosis after examining a slide. Fat necrosis might be found in which one of the following situations?","type":"Short Answer","subject":"General Pathology","topic":"General and Systemic Pathology","topicOriginal":"General and Systemic Pathology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Pathology","displayTopic":"General and Systemic Pathology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-481cf6c552b0","stem":"8 A healthy 26-year-old man fractured his right tibia in a road traffic accident. His right leg was immobilised in a plaster cast. The cast was removed from his leg after 8 weeks of immobilisation. Which of the following changes is most likely to have taken place in his gastrocnemius muscle after this time?","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Head and Neck","topicOriginal":"Head and Neck","subtopic":"Ear","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Head and Neck","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-e99005e2e5cd","stem":"9 A 21-year-old man sustained a severe soft-tissue injury following a road traffic accident. Which of the following metabolic effects is most likely to follow this injury?","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Medical Biochemistry","topic":"Proteins and Enzymes","topicOriginal":"Proteins and Enzymes","subtopic":"Protein","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Medical Biochemistry","displayTopic":"Proteins and Enzymes","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-5bd0eb812d6a","stem":"11 A 15-year-old girl with haemophilia A has had episodes of pain in her knees for the past 6 years. Over time, there has been an increase in size of her knee joints, with deformity. Laboratory studies show decreased levels of coagulation factor VIII activity. Which of the following is most likely to be seen within the joint space following episodes of pain?","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Head and Neck","topicOriginal":"Head and Neck","subtopic":"Ear","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Head and Neck","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b9209b15eb58","stem":"12 A 42-year-old woman has complained of mild, burning, substernal or epigastric pain following meals for the past 3 years. Upper gastrointestinal endoscopy is performed and biopsies are taken of an erythematous area of the lower oesophageal mucosa 3 cm above the gastro-oesophageal junction. There is no mass lesion, no ulceration, and no haemorrhage is noted. The biopsies injury demonstrate the presence of columnar epithelium with goblet cells. Which of the following mucosal cell alterations is most likely to be represented by these findings?","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Histology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Histology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-fa12bc1d598b","stem":"13 A 62-year-old diabetic and hypertensive man suffered a stroke which affected his speech and movement in the right arm and leg. A cerebral angiogram revealed an occlusion of his left middle cerebral artery. Months later, a computed tomographic (CT) scan shows a large, 5-cm cystic area in his left parietal lobe cortex. This CT finding most likely demonstrates a lesion that is the consequence of resolution of which of the following events?","type":"Clinical Vignette","subject":"General Pathology","topic":"General and Systemic Pathology","topicOriginal":"General and Systemic Pathology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Pathology","displayTopic":"General and Systemic Pathology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-1c15e647d7f7","stem":"14 A 25-year-old woman breastfed her first baby for almost 1 year with no difficulties and no complications. Which of the following cellular processes that occurred in the breast during pregnancy allowed her to nurse the infant for this period of time?","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Histology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Histology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-9fd2ea5bf18a","stem":"15 An 80-year-old woman was found dead in her room in a nursing home one morning. An autopsy was carried out and her death was reported as being secondary to old age. At autopsy, her heart was small (250 g) and dark-brown in colour on section. Microscopically, there was light-brown perinuclear pigment seen after haematoxylin and eosin (H&E) staining of the cardiac muscle fibres. Which of the following substances is most likely to be increased in the myocardial fibres to produce this cardiac appearance?","type":"Short Answer","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-173a730d0a6e","stem":"16 A histopathologist examining a slide used a series of immunohistochemical stains to identify different cellular components. One particular stain identified the presence of intermediate filaments within cells. This cytokeratin stain is most likely to be useful for which of the following diagnostic purposes?","type":"Clinical Vignette","subject":"General Pathology","topic":"General and Systemic Pathology","topicOriginal":"General and Systemic Pathology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Pathology","displayTopic":"General and Systemic Pathology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-d8e4b96c88e1","stem":"17 A 73-year-old woman with long-standing hypertension and aortic stenosis died suddenly one morning. An autopsy was performed on her body. At autopsy, her heart weighed 540 g. The size of her heart is most likely to be the result of which of the following processes involving the myocardial fibres?","type":"Short Answer","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-1e9d49404fee","stem":"18 A 28-year-old woman developed a darker skin complexion after returning from a holiday trip to Goa. Her skin did not show warmth, erythema or tenderness. Her skin tone faded to its original appearance within 1 month. Which of the following substances contributes mostcell to the biochemical process leading to these skin changes?","type":"Short Answer","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-8b805b881742","stem":"19 Metaplasia is a reversible change in which one adult cell type (epithelial or mesenchymal) is replaced by another adult cell type. In which of the following situations is the process of epithelial metaplasia most likely to have occurred?","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Histology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Histology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-d32a48797a20","stem":"20 A histopathologist reviewing a slide noticed a disease process which has led to scattered loss of individual cells, with the microscopic appearance of karyorrhexis and cell fragmentation. The overall tissue structure, however, has remained intact. This process is most typical of which of the following diseases?","type":"Short Answer","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"